<title>BELGIUM: Farm ministers seek precautions against flower imports.</title>
<headline>Farm ministers seek precautions against flower imports.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tariff quota increases for imports of flowers and plants should reflect EU demand and the importance of local production, EU farm ministers concluded.</p>
<p>In a statement approving a report on the impact third country trade agreements can have on the European Union's flower and plant trade, ministers made several other demands.</p>
<p>Imports should also be seasonally adjusted and plant health standards should be mutually respected.</p>
<p>Import policies for African, Caribbean and Pacific (ACP) countries and under the Generalised System of Preferences (GSP) should be brought into line with those applied to other countries.</p>
<p>EU flower and plant growers have expressed concern about the detrimental effect of preferential trade agreements on their their business.</p>
</text>
